#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is inspired by and based upon research conducted at Cleveland Clinic, as described in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exposing the full workflow for implicit solvent calculations and extending it with iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, and automatic qubit layout selection. Please refer to the [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), jointly developed by Cleveland Clinic and IBM&reg; based on Cleveland Clinic research, for a streamlined, black-box interface for running implicit solvent calculations.\n"
msgstr "Este tutorial é inspirado e baseado em pesquisa conduzida na Cleveland Clinic, conforme descrito em [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), expondo o fluxo de trabalho completo para cálculos de solvente implícito e estendendo-o com autoconsistência iterativa de solvente (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), otimização de geometria e seleção automática de layout de qubit. Consulte o [modelo de Função Qiskit SQD IEF-PCM](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), desenvolvido em conjunto pela Cleveland Clinic e pela IBM&reg; com base em pesquisa da Cleveland Clinic, para uma interface simplificada e \"caixa-preta\" para executar cálculos de solvente implícito.\n"

